    "traits": {
      "Celestial Revelation": {
        "text": "Undead Revelation. When you reach character level 3, you can transform as a Bonus Action into the Necrotic Shroud Form. The transformation lasts for 1 minute or until you end it (no action required). Once you transform, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.\n\nOnce on each of your turns before the transformation ends, you can deal extra damage to one target when you deal damage to it with an attack or a spell. The extra damage equals your Proficiency Bonus, and the extra damage's type is Necrotic.\n\nNecrotic Shroud. Your eyes briefly become pools of darkness, and flightless wings sprout from your back temporarily. Creatures other than your allies within 10 feet of you must succeed on a Charisma saving throw (DC 8 plus your Charisma modifier and Proficiency Bonus) or have the Frightened condition until the end of your next turn."
      },
      "Healing Hands": {
        "text": "Harming Hands. As a magic action, you can cast the Inflict Wounds spell. If you target yourself or an undead creature with Inflict Wounds, you instead heal them for 2d8 hit points instead of the spells normal damage. You can use this trait a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus per long rest."
      },
      "Celestial Resistance": {
        "text": "You have Resistance to Necrotic damage."
      }
    },
    "added": [
      {
        "id": "tmvoiqr95",
        "name": "Undead Nature",
        "level": 1,
        "desc": "You are immune to poison damage, and you can't be poisoned. You don't require air, food, drink, or sleep."
      },
      {
        "id": "tmvois0ew",
        "name": "Trance",
        "level": 1,
        "desc": "You don't need to sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep. You can finish a Long Rest in 4 hours if you spend those hours in a trancelike meditation, during which you retain consciousness."
      },
      {
        "id": "tmvsulygt",
